# Testing standards

## Requirements

- No real hardware, Core Location hardware, or network in unit tests
- Fake/manual seams: engine, permission, lifecycle, queue, path, schedulers, clock, device id, auth, transport
- Prefer behavior assertions (callbacks, queue contents, pending flags, encoded JSON keys)
- Cover success, failure, cancel/session invalidation, and empty/edge batches
- Keep tests `@MainActor` when exercising the facade or main-actor types

## Patterns

```swift
// ✅ Deterministic time
clock.now = clock.now.addingTimeInterval(timeout + 0.1)
absenceScheduler.fire()

// ❌ Sleeping for wall-clock window duration in unit tests
try await Task.sleep(for: .seconds(60))
```

- Use `BlockingQueue` when asserting in-flight durable writes / stop-finalize pending
- Encoding tests: assert JSON keys and `null` lat/lng; never require live IDFV
- Do not assert on private call order unless it is the bug under test

## Commands

Prefer package tests:

```bash
xcodebuild test -scheme SelectBeaconSDK-Package \
  -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17'
```
